,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kupang Malay - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kupang_Malay,"Kupang Malay or Kupang language is a Malay-based creole language spoken in Kupang, East Nusa Tenggara, which is on the west end of Timor Island. Kupang Malay is presently used as a lingua franca for inter-ethnic communication, and it also has native speakers.","Malay, Kupang",Creole
1,Malay trade and creole languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malay_trade_and_creole_languages,"Kupang Malay or Kupang language is a Malay-based creole language spoken in Kupang, East Nusa Tenggara, which is on the west end of Timor Island. Kupang Malay is presently used as a lingua franca for inter-ethnic communication, and it also has native speakers.","Malay, Kupang",Creole
2,Malay trade and creole languages - Wikipedia,https://web.archive.org/web/20220430013211/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malay_trade_and_creole_languages,Languages descended from Low Malay. Malay trade and creole languages. Bahasa-Bahasa Melayu Dagang dan Kreol.10.9Papuan/Irian Malay. 11Creole languages based on languages other than Malay. 12References. 13External links.,"Malay, Kupang",Creole
3,Kupang Malay — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kupang_malay,"Kupang Malay exhibits predominantly analytic morphology, with minimal inflection and a reliance on word-formation processes such as derivation, compounding, and reduplication, reflecting its development as a creole from Eastern Indonesian Trade Malay substrates.","Malay, Kupang",Creole
4,"Santesh | Satu Kupang | Medusa The Album | Official Music ...LORENSO AMAUNUT - TARIAN JAI - YouTubeMalay, Kupang - worldmission.mediaEastern Varieties of Indonesian (Kupang Malay, Ternate Malay ...",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mvF0lJ3xf9U,"See what others said about this video while it was live. (Playback ID: Y0ID99YH4Y7-tfJ4) Mar 21, 2025 · Kupang Malay, spoken by around 200,000 people in East Nusa Tenggara, Indonesia, is a Malay-based creole used in informal settings across the region. It represents a unique blend of Indonesian and local languages. Paul Bolla, a local journalist, started the column in 1992, which is written in Kupang Malay (also named Bahasa Kupang, Kupang language), a Malay-based creole spoken in and around the city of Kupang by approximately 220,000 native speakers and tens of thousands of second-language speakers (Jacob and Grimes 2006).... What is Kupang Malay? Kupang Malay is presently used as a lingua franca for inter-ethnic communication, and it also has native speakers. It is based on archaic Malay mixed mostly with Dutch, Portuguese, and other local languages. Is Makassar Malay a creole language? Makassar Malay is a creole-based mixed language, which is built of Bazaar Malay lexicon, Makassarese inflections, and mixed Malay/Makassarese syntax. It is now widely spoken as the first language in Makassar City and its surrounding areas, especially those who were born after the 1980s. What is Orang Pulo language? The Orang Pulo language (Logat Orang Pulo), alternatively known as Melayu Campuran (Mixed Malay) or Melayu Kepulauan Seribu (Thousand Islands Malay), is a Malay-based creole spoken by the Orang Pulo (lit. 'People of Island') inhabiting the Thousand Islands off the coast of Jakarta, Indonesia. What is Baba Malay? A kind of Baba Malay, locally called Peranakan from the ethnonym, the language is spoken among Chinese-Indonesians living in various regions of Indonesia, most visibly in Surabaya and Medan.","Malay, Kupang",Creole
5,"LORENSO AMAUNUT - TARIAN JAI - YouTubeMalay, Kupang - worldmission.mediaEastern Varieties of Indonesian (Kupang Malay, Ternate Malay ...",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HnHQnUQxbrk,"(Playback ID: Y0ID99YH4Y7-tfJ4) Mar 21, 2025 · Kupang Malay, spoken by around 200,000 people in East Nusa Tenggara, Indonesia, is a Malay-based creole used in informal settings across the region. It represents a unique blend of Indonesian and local languages. Paul Bolla, a local journalist, started the column in 1992, which is written in Kupang Malay (also named Bahasa Kupang, Kupang language), a Malay-based creole spoken in and around the city of Kupang by approximately 220,000 native speakers and tens of thousands of second-language speakers (Jacob and Grimes 2006).... What is Kupang Malay? Kupang Malay is presently used as a lingua franca for inter-ethnic communication, and it also has native speakers. It is based on archaic Malay mixed mostly with Dutch, Portuguese, and other local languages. Is Makassar Malay a creole language? Makassar Malay is a creole-based mixed language, which is built of Bazaar Malay lexicon, Makassarese inflections, and mixed Malay/Makassarese syntax. It is now widely spoken as the first language in Makassar City and its surrounding areas, especially those who were born after the 1980s. What is Orang Pulo language? The Orang Pulo language (Logat Orang Pulo), alternatively known as Melayu Campuran (Mixed Malay) or Melayu Kepulauan Seribu (Thousand Islands Malay), is a Malay-based creole spoken by the Orang Pulo (lit. 'People of Island') inhabiting the Thousand Islands off the coast of Jakarta, Indonesia. What is Baba Malay? A kind of Baba Malay, locally called Peranakan from the ethnonym, the language is spoken among Chinese-Indonesians living in various regions of Indonesia, most visibly in Surabaya and Medan.","Malay, Kupang",Creole
